uncharted 3 was important very important  and i'm going to tell you why  the year is 2011. gamers all over the  world are gushing over titles like  batman arkham city gears of war 3 and  the soon to be released elder scrolls 5  skyrim meanwhile a charismatic little  adventurer named nate is preparing to  make another big splash on sony's third  console but could that splash be bigger  than the one he made in 2009 november  1st 2021 marked the 10th anniversary of  uncharted 3 drake's deception and in the  decades since its release a lot has  changed naughty dog released the last of  us uncharted 4 uncharted lost legacy and  the last of us part 2 all of which  altered how we perceive the developer in  their own unique ways still uncharted 2  and 4 are widely held up as the best in  the series and for good reasons however  i'm here to tell you even though  uncharted 3 isn't the best it's the most  important for nate's development in this  video we're taking a look back at how  uncharted 3 lived up to its predecessor  what it did for the franchise and how it  holds up in a post uncharted 4 world for  more videos like this make sure to hit  the like button and subscribe to  gamespot  the 2009 spike video game award for game  of the year  goes to  uncharted 2 among themes  uncharted 2 among thieves was huge as  the title suggests it's the second  mainline game in the uncharted series  and received boatloads of critical  acclaim following its release in october  of 2009. nearly two years after  uncharted drake's fortune hit shelves  needless to say uncharted 2 is pretty  special and it stood as my favorite game  of all time until the witcher 3 and  breath of the wild came out but this  video isn't about link or geralt so  let's get back to nate just in case  you've never played an uncharted game  before let me summarize each game for  you in a very simple way  a man wants treasure so that man goes to  find the treasure but someone else wants  the treasure too so the man has to race  the other person to the treasure and  manages to defeat them just in the nick  of time it's a formula that doesn't  reinvent the wheel but it works as a  vehicle to drive the player to each new  string of fun dialogue and huge set  piece moments and uncharted 2 has both  of those elements in spades and most  importantly it doesn't include a jet ski  level  the success was without a doubt a great  thing for naughty dog but it also meant  that uncharted 3 had really big shoes to  fill so how could the dev keep this  momentum  going uncharted 3's development began in  2010 when for the first time naughty dog  split its dev team into two one team  worked on uncharted 3 while the other  worked on the last of us critically the  game reviewed very well grabbing a 9 out  of 10 from us here at gamespot and 10  out of 10 from sites like destructoid  and ign in terms of sales uncharted 3  blew past its predecessor and went on to  become the 4th best-selling ps3 game by  2015 the last of us being number 3 and  uncharted 2 being number 5. however  despite reviewing well and selling well  a quick google search will show you that  fan opinions of uncharted 3 are a bit  mixed some of this criticism includes  it's glitchy the hand-to-hand combat is  clunky it's more linear it's story makes  no sense and it's just more of the same  but i'd argue that not all of those  things are 100 true sure when you  compare the changes naughty dog made  from uncharted 1 to 2 with the changes  from 2-3 there isn't a whole lot to  speak of uncharted 2 improved gameplay  hand-to-hand combat grenade throwing  graphics added a little bit of stealth  elements as well as the grand spectacle  that was the cinematic cutscene like  gameplay moments but for what uncharted  3 lacks in terms of shiny new features  it makes up for with the story that  features nate looking more inward than  ever before if each entry boils down to  searching for treasure then uncharted 3  was the first to include the subtext of  nate searching for himself why is he  doing all of this what does he want  versus what does he need who is he  really it was the first game in the  series to give nate more of a backstory  and explain why he and sully put so much  trust in each other it stripped back  some of the campiness of the previous  two games and attempted to tell a  slightly more grounded story where the  characters could have important moments  like this one  i gotta say  i'm losing the plot here  remind me again why we're doing this  no no no no no if you're gearing up for  one of your i'm too old for this  speeches spare me  mate these guys are playing for keeps  yeah so  what you're just gonna roll over for  them nobody's talking about rolling over  then quit acting like you're ready to  lay down and die all right  listen kitten  i've had you back for 20 years  i'm not going anywhere  obviously  i just want to make sure we're doing  this for the right reasons  you got your pride all tangled up in  this thing it's making you reckless  i taught you better than that  the game's antagonist catherine marlow  isn't as threatening as some of the  others but she's a bit more calculated  and manipulative in the way she plays  with nate's head in a way she's like the  physical embodiment of nate's  consciousness  mind hell she even acts as his inner  voice later in the game after he loses  everything and wanders aimlessly through  the desert though my favorite line of  hers comes from her one-on-one talk with  nate where after poking the scars of his  past she plants a seed of distrust but  ask yourself  when he scooped you off the streets of  colombia 20 years ago  did he save you from that life  or did he just doom you to this one  and then there's elena possibly the most  important factor in nate's inner  struggle the story of uncharted 3 picks  up hot off the heels of nate and elena's  separation the two were married sometime  between the events of uc 2 and 3 but  things fell apart due to nate's lack of  commitment and lust for adventure this  conflict makes a return in uncharted 4  but it was here that we first got to see  the two clash in a different way than in  previous entries in uncharted 3 she's no  longer just elena begging him to hang it  up and walk away she's his estranged  wife asking him to decide what's more  important to him  what is wrong with you two elena come on  we're just joking around listen  you've won okay  you've outsmarted her  you know where to find the city and  marlow doesn't  why can't that be enough  [Music]  uncharted 3 may have felt like filler to  some and it might get slightly  overlooked because it sits between two  of the best in the series but without it  nate couldn't have become the man we see  in part 4.  so by now you're probably asking but  devante is it worth playing 10 years  later  yeah yeah it is even in a post uncharted  4 world with better graphics and tighter  gameplay uncharted 3 still manages to  shine the performances from nolan north  and the gang are rock solid making it  nearly impossible to not love these  characters the gameplay feels a little  rough in some spots such as the  hand-to-hand combat sequences the  wannabe stealth sections and the running  towards the camera stuff  but overall the complete package is just  as fun to play through as it ever was  and that's partly due to the game's  great level design which features series  gems like the chateau and the shipyard  these areas as well as the final escape  scene in the now classic plane moment  left me awestruck and eager for more but  it's not just the big moments that made  me feel like that it's also the calm  moments like getting to play as young  nate for the first time a moment that  wasn't really shown off in all of the  marketing and speaking of marketing  don't even get me started on uncharted  3's weird partnership with subway that  convinced me to go there way too many  times  subway where winners eat now it's crazy  to think about it but when uncharted 3  first released i was a 19 year old  college student dealing with keeping my  grades up and managing the heartbreak of  my crush being in love with my roommate  instead of me so sometimes my first  memories of the game can get a little  bit overshadowed by everything else i  was dealing with at the time however  when i put all of that aside i'm struck  with a sense of pride and nostalgia  pride because of how hard i worked to  pay for my ps3 so i wouldn't have to  borrow a friend's console like i'd done  with uncharted 2. and nostalgia because  the uncharted games meant so much to me  back then and still do to a certain  extent i can't even listen to the main  theme without getting a little  teary-eyed and just covered in  goosebumps  uncharted 3 drake's deception had some  big shoes to fill but it managed to live  up to those expectations by keeping  uncharted 2's award-winning formula and  putting nate through a transformative  experience it's hard to imagine nate's  journey without uncharted 3 and even 10  years later it's still a joy to play  thank you so much for watching i know  that this wasn't a ranked video but hit  the comment section and let me know how  you would rank the uncharted games and  feel free to include the mobile game or  golden abyss or even that trading card  game for vita yeah you remember that one  knock yourself out throw that into the  ranking and if you made it this far hit  the like button and subscribe so that  you know if and when uncharted 5 gets  announced  later  [Music]  you
 

